EXT. TREETOP MARKET, CANOPY OF THE WHISPERING WOOD - NOON

Rope bridges. Hanging stalls. Lanterns strung between giant branches. The market floats above the forest floor in green light.

QUILLON FERNWHISTLE (any age, mossy beard, one ear pointed) hawks charms from a swaying stall.

QUILLON
Lucky bones! Lucky bones!

BRAMBLE OAKENSHIELD-DIOP (30s, scarred forearm, an enormous axe on her back) pushes through the crowd, scanning every stall.

TILLY WREN-ABAYOMI (10, bare feet, a satchel too big for her) hops beside her, eating a honeyed fig.

BRAMBLE
Stay close, Tilly.

TILLY
I am close.

BRAMBLE
Closer.

QUILLON
Warrior-lady! Lucky bones for the child?

BRAMBLE
No.

QUILLON
Protection charms, then. Very cheap.

BRAMBLE
I said no.

Tilly tugs Bramble's sleeve. She points. At the far end of the bridge, a tall figure in a hooded cloak has stopped dead among the shoppers, looking directly at them.

TILLY
Bramble.

BRAMBLE
I see him.

QUILLON
(suddenly pale)
You'll want those bones after all.

The figure raises his head. Beneath the hood, no face: only a smooth plane of dark bark.

BRAMBLE
Run.

They bolt. The crowd parts. Behind them the hooded figure walks, calmly, as the ropes of the bridge begin to creak, then snap, one by one.

TILLY
(laughing, terrified)
Bramble, he's chasing us!

BRAMBLE
I noticed!

Quillon grabs a lantern, a bundle of bones, and scrambles up the nearest branch. The bridge drops. Bramble leaps, catches a rope, hauls Tilly up beside her, and swings them both onto a platform of woven vines.

They land in a heap, gasping, safe. Below, the hooded figure stands at the broken end of the bridge, looking up. Then it turns and walks away through empty air, and the forest swallows it.

TILLY
Do you think he'll come back?

BRAMBLE
Everything comes back.

QUILLON
(from above)
Lucky bones, anyone?
